 Riemann series, the variance is dominated by the tail. Cites E3.1, E1.5, S193 row 810, S194 row 814, Galway 2004, Hiary 2011, Montgomery 1973, Odlyzko 1989, Dyson sine-kernel. Cross-domain ingredient: GUE statistics of zero spacings + asymptotic li-expansion + Gaussian CLT applied to the truncation tail — first time the project has used random-matrix-theoretic equidistribution to PREDICT a quantitative empirical curve (not just bound it). **Falsifier**: a K-policy whose empirical median |err| stays bounded as x → ∞, OR a smoothing that drops the unsmoothed-K* below polylog, OR a rigorous calculation showing GUE correlation reduces K* below x · log^{-c}(x) for any c > 0. None known. See `experiments/analytic/connes_amortisation/gue_heuristic.py`, `gue_heuristic_results.md`. | 195 |
